     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Sunday, March 13, 2016 at 12:58:54 PM UTC-4, Stephan Schlögl wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Btw. &quot;Datei oder Verzeichnis nicht gefunden&quot; just means &quot;File or directory not found&quot;<br><br>On Sunday, March 13, 2016 at 2:15:54 PM UTC+1, Stephan Schlögl wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Hi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>I&#39;m trying to install shiny on a debian machine and I&#39;m running into the issue below...<br><br></span></div></code></div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Reading</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">package</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lists</span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Done</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Building</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dependency tree        <br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Reading</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> state information</span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Done</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Building</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data structures</span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Done</span><span style=\"color:#000